{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "באש תשרף", :translit "ba'esh tisaref", :gloss "with fire she shall be burned"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Lexical-thematic link: the element of fire in the daughter's execution mirrors the fire that defines the priestly service."}], :frame {:text "The priestly service is centered on fire: the daily tamid offering is described as a continual burnt-offering kindled upon the altar (Exodus 29:42), and the altar's fire is to be kept perpetually burning (Leviticus 6:6). The daughter of a priest who profanes herself through harlotry is sentenced to burning (Leviticus 21:9). Ba'al HaTurim connects the mode of her execution to the element that defines her father's avoda.", :sources ["Exodus 29:42" "Leviticus 6:6" "Leviticus 21:9"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Lexical-thematic link: the element of fire in the daughter's execution mirrors the fire that defines the priestly service.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:43.387346742Z", :model "glm-5.2"}